WEBVTT

00:29:59.542 --> 00:30:03.143
but also to help them understand
where that sweet spot was.

00:30:03.167 --> 00:30:06.309
AG: But that sweet spot
was different for each country.

00:30:06.333 --> 00:30:08.684
One of the best ways
to understand the other side

00:30:08.708 --> 00:30:11.393
is to ask them questions about the future.

00:30:11.417 --> 00:30:13.226
Not just what their goals are today,

00:30:13.250 --> 00:30:16.917
but what they're hoping to accomplish
in the next few months or even years.

00:30:17.738 --> 00:30:19.643
There's evidence that expert negotiators

00:30:19.667 --> 00:30:21.893
dedicate more than
twice as much planning time

00:30:21.917 --> 00:30:24.268
to long-term considerations
as their peers.

00:30:24.292 --> 00:30:26.434
The further you stretch out
the time horizon,

00:30:26.458 --> 00:30:28.351
the less fixed the pie becomes

00:30:28.375 --> 00:30:31.708
and the more possibilities you can
sketch out for helping one another.